---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  page="privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy – COGNAK"
  description="How COGNAK handles data, analytics, advertising, and cookies on cognak.com."
  ogUrl="https://cognak.com/privacy-policy/"
  pageBg="#F1D6EA"
>
  <canvas id="privacy-grid" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

  <main id="cognak-main"><section class="privacy-template">

    <h1 class="privacy-headline">Our <span class="pp-lead"><span class="pp-accent">privacy policy</span>,</span> minus the legalese.</h1>

    <div class="privacy-body">
      <p>COGNAK LLC is a design and development studio based in Los Angeles, California. This page explains how we handle data when you visit cognak.com.</p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <div class="pp-gloss">We count visits, not people.</div>
      <p>We use Google Analytics (GA4) to collect anonymous, aggregate data about how visitors use this site: pages visited, session duration, and general geographic region. This data is never linked to any individual and is not sold or shared with third parties.</p>
      <p>We also run Google Ads to advertise our services. If you accept cookies, Google Ads may set cookies to measure whether an ad led to a visit or inquiry, and to improve the relevance of ads you see. No personally identifiable information is collected or shared.</p>
      <p>You can opt out of Google Analytics tracking at any time using the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>. You can manage Google ad personalization at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">adssettings.google.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <div class="pp-gloss">Nothing is set until you say yes.</div>
      <p>Every cookie this site can set, what it does, and how long it lasts. All tracking is consent-gated. Declining prevents any analytics or ad cookie from being set at all.</p>

      {/* Deliberately a <div>, not a <p> or <table>: custom.css sets
          `html.js .privacy-body p` to opacity:0 awaiting the word-stagger,
          which only reveals elements listed in cognak-global.js's SELECTORS.
          A new <p> here would be invisible forever — the bug that shipped on
          /send. Grid rather than <table> to match the colophon spec block's
          construction and to stack cleanly on mobile. */}
      <div class="pp-cookies">
        <div class="pp-ck-head">Cookie</div>
        <div class="pp-ck-head">Set by</div>
        <div class="pp-ck-head">Purpose</div>
        <div class="pp-ck-head">Lifetime</div>

        <div class="pp-ck-name" data-label="Cookie">cognak_consent</div>
        <div data-label="Set by">COGNAK</div>
        <div data-label="Purpose">Remembers this choice</div>
        <div data-label="Lifetime">1 year</div>

        <div class="pp-ck-name" data-label="Cookie">_ga</div>
        <div data-label="Set by">Google Analytics</div>
        <div data-label="Purpose">Tells return visits apart</div>
        <div data-label="Lifetime">2 years</div>

        <div class="pp-ck-name" data-label="Cookie">_ga_*</div>
        <div data-label="Set by">Google Analytics</div>
        <div data-label="Purpose">Keeps session state</div>
        <div data-label="Lifetime">2 years</div>

        <div class="pp-ck-name" data-label="Cookie">_gcl_*</div>
        <div data-label="Set by">Google Ads</div>
        <div data-label="Purpose">Measures ad conversions</div>
        <div data-label="Lifetime">90 days</div>
      </div>

      <p class="pp-cookies-note">Only <code>cognak_consent</code> is ours, and it is the only one set if you decline. The rest appear solely after you accept.</p>

      {/* JS-gated in CSS: with no JS this can't read your cookie, and a
          control that reports a state it can't verify is worse than none.
          The ledger above stays visible either way. */}
      <div class="pp-consent" id="pp-consent" hidden>
        <span class="pp-consent-label">Your current choice:</span>
        <span class="pp-consent-state" id="pp-consent-state">—</span>
        <span class="pp-consent-actions" id="pp-consent-actions"></span>
      </div>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <div class="pp-gloss">Your email is used to reply, and nothing else.</div>
      <p>If you reach out via hello@cognak.com, your email and message are used solely to respond to your inquiry. No information is stored beyond standard email retention.</p>

      <h2>Your Rights</h2>
      <div class="pp-gloss">Ask, and we delete it.</div>
      <p>EU visitors may request access to or deletion of any personal data we hold by contacting <a href="mailto:hello@cognak.com">hello@cognak.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
      <div class="pp-gloss">The work here isn't yours to reuse.</div>
      <p>All work, imagery, and content displayed on cognak.com is the property of COGNAK LLC or its respective clients and is protected by copyright. Nothing on this site may be reproduced, copied, or redistributed without prior written permission from COGNAK LLC.</p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p><a href="mailto:hello@cognak.com">hello@cognak.com</a></p>
    </div>

  </section></main>

  <style is:inline>
    html, body { background-color: #F1D6EA !important; }
    .privacy-template { background-color: transparent !important; }
    .privacy-headline .pp-accent { color: #6E2050; }
    /* Keep "privacy policy," together so the comma never wraps to the next line
       (the word-splitter would otherwise make the comma its own wrapping box). */
    .privacy-headline .pp-lead { white-space: nowrap; }

    #privacy-grid {
      position: fixed;
      inset: 0;
      width: 100vw;
      height: 100vh;
      z-index: 0;
      pointer-events: none;
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(6px);
      transition: opacity 0.9s var(--ease-standard), transform 0.9s var(--ease-standard);
    }
    #privacy-grid.is-in {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      #privacy-grid {
        opacity: 1;
        transform: none;
        transition: none;
      }
    }
    #cognak-main { position: relative; z-index: 1; }

    /* ---- plain-English glosses --------------------------------------------
       The headline promises "minus the legalese" and the prose underneath,
       while readable, is still policy prose. These are the payoff: one line
       per section. Someone who skims only these five lines should still leave
       correctly informed.

       REVISED 2026-07-31 (Pierce), twice: was mono 12px behind a hairline left
       rule with a stacked uppercase "IN SHORT" eyebrow — an aside. Then bold
       body copy prefixed "In short:". Now just the bold sentence, no label at
       all: the page's whole promise is "minus the legalese", so announcing a
       plain-English summary implied there was legalese to summarise. The line
       is short, bold and first — it doesn't need to introduce itself.
       The rule, the mono and the label are all gone deliberately; don't
       reinstate any of them.

       06 Questions deliberately has none — it's a single email address, and
       glossing it would be padding to complete a pattern.

       A <div>, not a <p>: `html.js .privacy-body p` is held at opacity:0 for
       the word-stagger, which only reveals what's in its SELECTORS list. */
    .pp-gloss {
      font-family: 'Diatype Variable', sans-serif;
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: 700;
      /* Matches .privacy-body p exactly (16px / 1.8) — the gloss now reads as
         an emphasized first line of the section rather than a marginal note,
         so it has to sit on the same baseline rhythm as the prose it leads. */
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: #3A313B;
      margin: 0 0 28.8px; /* 1x the 28.8px baseline grid — see custom.css */
    }


    /* ---- cookie ledger ----------------------------------------------------
       Hairline mono table, built as a grid so it stacks on mobile (a real
       <table> can't). Same construction as the colophon spec block. */
    .pp-cookies {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: max-content max-content 1fr max-content;
      gap: 0.55rem 1.6rem;
      align-items: baseline;
      font-family: 'Diatype Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 12px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #3A313B;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(129,82,117,0.35);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(129,82,117,0.35);
      padding: 1.4rem 0;
      margin: 0 0 28.8px; /* 1x */
    }
    .pp-ck-head {
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      font-size: 10px;
      color: rgba(129,82,117,0.75);
    }
    .pp-ck-name { color: #815275; }
    .pp-cookies-note { font-size: 14px !important; color: #6b5f6b !important; }

    /* Stacked on narrow screens: each cell reintroduces its column header from
       the data-label, and the header row itself is dropped. */
    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .pp-cookies { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; }
      .pp-ck-head { display: none; }
      .pp-cookies > div[data-label] { padding: 1px 0; }
      .pp-cookies > div[data-label]::before {
        content: attr(data-label) ' \00B7 ';
        color: rgba(129,82,117,0.6);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.1em;
        font-size: 10px;
      }
      /* Gap between stacked records. Applied to every name cell including the
         first — :first-of-type would match the first DIV among siblings, which
         is a .pp-ck-head, so it would never hit a name cell anyway, and the
         box already has 1.4rem of padding above the first row. */
      .pp-cookies > .pp-ck-name { margin-top: 1rem; }
    }

    /* ---- live consent readout ---------------------------------------------
       Hidden until JS confirms it can actually read the cookie (the [hidden]
       attribute comes off in script). No-JS keeps the ledger and loses only
       the control, which is the honest failure mode. */
    .pp-consent {
      font-family: 'Diatype Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 12px;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      line-height: 1.9;
      color: #3A313B;
      margin: 0 0 28.8px; /* 1x */
    }
    .pp-consent-label { text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(129,82,117,0.75); letter-spacing: 0.12em; font-size: 10px; }
    .pp-consent-state { text-transform: uppercase; color: #815275; font-weight: 500; margin: 0 0.15em 0 0.4em; }
    .pp-consent-actions button {
      font: inherit;
      background: none;
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
      margin-left: 0.9em;
      color: #3A313B;
      cursor: pointer;
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: var(--link-offset);
      text-decoration-color: rgba(var(--link-ink-rgb), 0.3);
      transition: color var(--link-dur) var(--link-ease), text-decoration-color var(--link-dur) var(--link-ease);
    }
    @media (hover: hover) {
      .pp-consent-actions button:hover { color: #815275; text-decoration-color: #815275; }
    }
    /* Confirmation beat after a change — the state word pulses once so the
       click has a visible consequence beyond the word swapping. */
    .pp-consent-state.is-changed { animation: pp-consent-pulse 0.9s var(--ease-standard); }
    @keyframes pp-consent-pulse {
      0%   { background: rgba(129,82,117,0.28); }
      100% { background: rgba(129,82,117,0); }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .pp-consent-state.is-changed { animation: none; }
    }
  </style>

  <script is:inline>
    if (history.scrollRestoration) { history.scrollRestoration = 'manual'; }
    window.scrollTo(0, 0);
    /* Headline + body text reveal is handled by the site-wide word-stagger in
       cognak-global.js (same as projects/studio) — no local observer here. */
  </script>

  <script is:inline>
    /* ---------------------------------------------- live consent readout ---
       Reads cognak_consent and lets you change it from here.

       This is the ONLY way to change your mind on the whole site: the banner
       in BaseLayout hides itself permanently once the cookie exists
       (`if (document.cookie.indexOf('cognak_consent=') !== -1) ... display =
       none`), so an accepted visitor was accepted forever with no exit.

       Two things the banner doesn't have to do, which this must:
       1. Send an explicit DENIED consent update. The banner's decline path
          skips it because consent mode already defaults to denied — but
          accepted -> declined is a real transition and has to be sent.
       2. Clear the cookies already on disk. Declining after having accepted
          leaves _ga / _ga_* / _gcl_* sitting there; on this page of all
          pages, saying "declined" while they persist would be a lie.

       Cookie name and expiry are duplicated from BaseLayout's banner — if
       either changes, change it in both places. */
    (function () {
      var wrap = document.getElementById('pp-consent');
      if (!wrap) return;

      var stateEl = document.getElementById('pp-consent-state');
      var actionsEl = document.getElementById('pp-consent-actions');

      function read() {
        var m = document.cookie.match(/(?:^|;\s*)cognak_consent=([^;]*)/);
        return m ? m[1] : '';
      }

      function write(val) {
        var d = new Date();
        d.setFullYear(d.getFullYear() + 1);
        document.cookie = 'cognak_consent=' + val + ';expires=' + d.toUTCString() + ';path=/;SameSite=Lax';
      }

      /* GA/Ads cookies are JS-set (not HttpOnly), so they're expirable from
         here — but only with a matching domain attribute, and GA writes _ga on
         the registrable domain while some are written host-only. Rather than
         guess, expire each name against every plausible domain variant; the
         ones that don't match are no-ops. */
      function clearAnalyticsCookies() {
        var host = location.hostname;
        var parts = host.split('.');
        var domains = ['', host, '.' + host];
        if (parts.length > 2) {
          var root = parts.slice(-2).join('.');
          domains.push(root, '.' + root);
        }
        var names = document.cookie.split(';').map(function (c) {
          return c.split('=')[0].trim();
        }).filter(function (n) {
          return n && (n === '_ga' || n.indexOf('_ga_') === 0 || n.indexOf('_gcl') === 0 || n.indexOf('_gid') === 0);
        });
        names.forEach(function (n) {
          domains.forEach(function (dom) {
            document.cookie = n + '=;expires=Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 GMT;path=/' +
                              (dom ? ';domain=' + dom : '');
          });
        });
      }

      var GRANTED = {
        analytics_storage: 'granted', ad_storage: 'granted',
        ad_user_data: 'granted', ad_personalization: 'granted'
      };
      var DENIED = {
        analytics_storage: 'denied', ad_storage: 'denied',
        ad_user_data: 'denied', ad_personalization: 'denied'
      };

      function set(val, announce) {
        write(val);
        try {
          if (typeof gtag === 'function') {
            gtag('consent', 'update', val === 'accepted' ? GRANTED : DENIED);
          }
        } catch (e) {}
        if (val === 'declined') clearAnalyticsCookies();
        render(announce);
      }

      function button(label, val) {
        var b = document.createElement('button');
        b.type = 'button';
        b.textContent = label;
        b.addEventListener('click', function () { set(val, true); });
        return b;
      }

      function render(announce) {
        var v = read();
        stateEl.textContent = v === 'accepted' ? 'Accepted'
                            : v === 'declined' ? 'Declined'
                            : 'Not set';
        actionsEl.textContent = '';
        if (v === 'accepted') {
          actionsEl.appendChild(button('decline instead', 'declined'));
        } else if (v === 'declined') {
          actionsEl.appendChild(button('accept instead', 'accepted'));
        } else {
          actionsEl.appendChild(button('accept', 'accepted'));
          actionsEl.appendChild(button('decline', 'declined'));
        }
        if (announce) {
          stateEl.classList.remove('is-changed');
          // Reflow so the animation restarts on a repeat change.
          void stateEl.offsetWidth;
          stateEl.classList.add('is-changed');
        }
      }

      render(false);
      wrap.hidden = false;
    })();
  </script>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var canvas = document.getElementById('privacy-grid');
      if (!canvas || !canvas.getContext) return;
      var ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
      var reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      var touch = window.matchMedia('(hover: none)').matches;

      var dpr = 1, vw = 0, vh = 0, spacing = 28.8, gridPhase = 0;
      function resize() {
        dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
        vw = window.innerWidth;
        vh = window.innerHeight;
        canvas.width = Math.round(vw * dpr);
        canvas.height = Math.round(vh * dpr);
        var p = document.querySelector('.privacy-body p');
        if (p) {
          var cs = getComputedStyle(p);
          var lh = parseFloat(cs.lineHeight);
          if (lh > 8) spacing = lh;

          /* Phase the ruled lines onto the text's actual BASELINES instead of
             an arbitrary origin at the top of the document. The margins in
             custom.css are quantized to `spacing`, so once the first baseline
             is on a rule every following line stays on one.

             Aligning the grid to the type (rather than pushing the type to fit
             an arbitrary grid) keeps the layout untouched — the rules are
             decoration, the copy is not.

             Baseline position inside a line box is (leading / 2) + ascent.
             fontBoundingBox* comes from the font's own metrics, so it's stable
             across strings; the 0.8em fallback is for engines that don't
             report it. */
          var asc, desc;
          try {
            ctx.font = cs.fontStyle + ' ' + cs.fontWeight + ' ' + cs.fontSize + ' ' + cs.fontFamily;
            var m = ctx.measureText('x');
            asc = m.fontBoundingBoxAscent;
            desc = m.fontBoundingBoxDescent;
          } catch (e) {}
          var fs = parseFloat(cs.fontSize) || 16;
          var baselineInBox = (asc && desc)
            ? (spacing - (asc + desc)) / 2 + asc
            : (spacing - fs) / 2 + fs * 0.8;

          var top = p.getBoundingClientRect().top + (window.scrollY || 0);
          gridPhase = (top + baselineInBox) % spacing;
        }
      }
      resize();
      window.addEventListener('resize', resize);

      var mx = -9999, my = -9999, tx = -9999, ty = -9999;
      if (!touch) {
        window.addEventListener('mousemove', function (e) { tx = e.clientX; ty = e.clientY; });
        document.addEventListener('mouseleave', function () { tx = -9999; ty = -9999; });
      }

      var SIGMA = 95, AMP = 7, STEP = 22;

      function drawLine(y, alpha, rippling) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(129,82,117,' + alpha + ')';
        ctx.beginPath();
        if (!rippling || my < -999 || Math.abs(y - my) > SIGMA * 2.2) {
          ctx.moveTo(0, y);
          ctx.lineTo(vw, y);
        } else {
          var first = true;
          for (var x = 0; x <= vw + STEP; x += STEP) {
            var dx = x - mx, dy = y - my;
            var d2 = dx * dx + dy * dy;
            var off = -AMP * Math.sign(dy || 1) * Math.exp(-d2 / (2 * SIGMA * SIGMA));
            if (first) { ctx.moveTo(x, y + off); first = false; }
            else ctx.lineTo(x, y + off);
          }
        }
        ctx.stroke();
      }

      function cropMark(x, y) {
        var L = 9, G = 4;
        ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(74,40,64,0.35)';
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(x - G - L, y); ctx.lineTo(x - G, y);
        ctx.moveTo(x + G, y); ctx.lineTo(x + G + L, y);
        ctx.moveTo(x, y - G - L); ctx.lineTo(x, y - G);
        ctx.moveTo(x, y + G); ctx.lineTo(x, y + G + L);
        ctx.stroke();
      }

      function frame(now) {
        ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
        ctx.clearRect(0, 0, vw, vh);
        ctx.lineWidth = 1;

        mx += (tx - mx) * 0.12;
        my += (ty - my) * 0.12;

        var scrollY = window.scrollY || 0;
        // Modulo twice: the inner result can be negative (scrollY > gridPhase),
        // and a negative start would skip the first rule.
        var offset = (((gridPhase - scrollY) % spacing) + spacing) % spacing;
        var t = now * 0.001;

        for (var y = offset - spacing; y < vh + spacing; y += spacing) {
          var breath = reduced ? 1 : (0.7 + 0.3 * Math.sin(t * 0.45 - y * 0.006));
          drawLine(y, 0.065 * breath, !reduced && !touch);
        }

        var body = document.querySelector('.privacy-body');
        if (body) {
          var r = body.getBoundingClientRect();
          var ga = reduced ? 0.20 : (0.16 + 0.07 * Math.sin(t * 0.3));
          ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(129,82,117,' + ga + ')';
          ctx.beginPath();
          ctx.moveTo(r.left - 24, 0); ctx.lineTo(r.left - 24, vh);
          ctx.moveTo(r.right + 24, 0); ctx.lineTo(r.right + 24, vh);
          ctx.stroke();

          var head = document.querySelector('.privacy-headline');
          if (head) {
            var hr = head.getBoundingClientRect();
            cropMark(r.left - 24, hr.top - 18);
            cropMark(r.right + 24, hr.top - 18);
          }
          cropMark(r.left - 24, r.bottom + 26);
          cropMark(r.right + 24, r.bottom + 26);
        }

        if (!reduced) requestAnimationFrame(frame);
      }

      /* The phase depends on where the first paragraph lands, which depends on
         the headline's height, which depends on the webfont. Measuring only at
         script time would lock in the fallback-font layout and leave the rules
         a few px off every baseline once Diatype swaps in. */
      function remeasure() {
        resize();
        if (reduced) frame(performance.now());
      }
      if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) {
        document.fonts.ready.then(remeasure).catch(function () {});
      }
      window.addEventListener('load', remeasure);

      requestAnimationFrame(function (now) {
        frame(now);
        canvas.classList.add('is-in');
      });
      if (reduced) {
        window.addEventListener('resize', function () { frame(performance.now()); });
        window.addEventListener('scroll', function () { frame(performance.now()); }, { passive: true });
      }
    })();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
